4. Prove the unattended Remote lifecycle on owned fixtures: install, enable, pair once, outbound reconnect, select computer, receive fresh timestamped pictures, send an arbitrary prompt, execute with real local Windows authority, observe progress/results/errors/receipts, and exercise Stop, Pause, Disable, rotation, Revoke, expiry, duplication, stale state, interruption, locked-session, UAC, and network-recovery boundaries without private leakage.
5. After the separate MemoryEndpoints DESIGN and RELEASE acceptances exist, implement and prove the Memory swarm on two independently installed Connect instances: two distinct active names and memories work concurrently; duplicate normalized name loses; the same immutable memory cannot gain a second writer across path/computer changes; a true branch gets a new identity and complete lineage; renewal, expiry, takeover, reconnect, restart, and every stale mutation fail with deterministic receipts and no side effects.
6. Prove authenticated UI and Demo parity through the same renderers, controls, validation, and client methods, with unmistakable session-local mock data, clean scene routes, accessible overlays, screenshots, keyboard/reduced-motion/forced-colors behavior, narrow-screen reflow, privacy containment, and guarded zero-protected-request assertions.
7. Recheck SEO, canonical URLs, structured data, crawler files, OpenAPI, manifests, route inventory, release logs, package/download trust copy, and public claims across all sites so every surface describes the same verified architecture and every remaining unknown is visibly labeled.

## Regular check-in and deployment cadence

- Treat source check-in and site deployment as recurring operating duties for every product in the five-product matrix, not as a one-time cleanup. Recheck each owning root at the start and end of every work session, after every independently verified vertical slice, and before every handoff or context reset.
- When a coherent source slice has SOURCE GO and its exact owning repository and origin are known, commit and push those exact reviewed bytes promptly. Never leave accepted work indefinitely only in a dirty tree, combine unrelated roots in one commit, manufacture history for a directory without Git authority, or describe an unpushed commit as checked in.
- After each accepted check-in, rerun the clean-tree package and deployment admission gates for that exact revision. Deploy every site whose immutable PACKAGE and target-bound DEPLOYMENT gates are GO, then verify the exact live revision plus health, release, contract, and required behavioral routes. A deployment is not complete until the sanitized activation receipt and post-activation LIVE checks bind the target to the accepted revision.
- Maintain an explicit per-product ledger in this file on every pass: authoritative root, branch/revision, dirty/ahead/behind state, SOURCE/PACKAGE/INSTALLED/DEPLOYMENT/LIVE verdicts, last verified live revision, exact blocker, owning boundary, and next executable action. If a site cannot be checked in or deployed, record the named missing authority and continue the other independent products; never silently skip it and never force an unsafe deployment.
- The present exceptions are deliberate and must be rechecked rather than normalized: RemoteEndpoints has no supplied Git history/origin; the public Multi-Agent-Memory checkout has no target-bound `multiagentmemory` deployment profile; the private commercial MemoryEndpoints source/deployment boundary is absent from this checkout; LocalEndpoints lacks the qualified production runtime/atomic activation path; and Connect lacks whole-SOURCE acceptance plus an admissible privacy-clean signed package. These are current blockers, not permission to stop pursuing regular check-in and deployment.

## Cold-start continuation sequence

1. Read `AGENTS.md`, then `.uai/startup-packet.uai`, then every file in the packet's complete declared order. After the governed repository startup manifest is loaded, read this cross-product `workspace.uai` coordinator checkpoint; it is intentionally outside that manifest. Inspect active handoff buckets before broad work.
2. Run `git status`, resolve the authoritative root and branch, fetch current refs read-only, and compare current bytes with the newest exact independent report. Preserve all other agents' and human changes.
3. Query the current public version, release, health, Demo, and contract routes. Record SOURCE, PACKAGE, INSTALLED, DEPLOYMENT, and LIVE independently.
4. Search the shared Improvement handoff for the newest report for the exact subsystem and gate. Treat older source packages and synthetic/debug artifacts as historical evidence only.
5. When authenticated MemoryEndpoints coordination is available, check current-message and project rooms, acknowledge handled notifications, use a unique agent identity, and acquire the required project/path or writer lease before shared mutation. If it is unavailable, continue from local `.uai` and public-safe handoff evidence without requesting or exposing a credential.
6. Prefer implementation and direct verification over another design memo. Stop at the first failed release gate, preserve exact public-safe evidence, remediate the owning source cleanly, and rerun from fresh frozen bytes.

## Required Next Prompt

### Feature/improvement focus

Continue the world-class unattended RemoteEndpoints, LocalEndpoint Connect, and MemoryEndpoints integration from the first unclosed gate above. Preserve one-time standing remote authority, exact authenticated/Demo UI parity, full plugin power, globally unique active swarm names, exclusive immutable-memory writers, and true concurrent branches without legacy support or claim inflation.

### Code/source changes

Reconcile the authoritative source and contract before modifying code. Implement the smallest complete vertical slice in its owning repository, update every dogfood consumer to the one current contract, remove superseded behavior in the same change, and keep credentials, private payloads, pictures, identifiers, packages, and deployment evidence out of public source.

### Automated tests/checks

Run focused tests first, then each owning repository's complete source, lint, build, browser, accessibility, privacy, package, signing, installed-byte, deployment-receipt, and live-revision gates required by the changed slice. Obtain independent SOURCE, PACKAGE, INSTALLED, DEPLOYMENT, and LIVE verdicts separately and never promote a partial GO into platform completion.
